Open Certificate Standard — specification licence
=================================================

The specification text in this repository is licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0

    Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
    Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt this specification for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and
indicate whether changes were made.

WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT GRANT

It does not permit you to describe a product as conforming to, or certified
against, this standard without having run the conformance criteria. A
conformance claim must state the version of the standard, the level claimed,
the certificate types covered, the date, and who is making the claim.

CODE AND TEST VECTORS ARE LICENSED SEPARATELY

Everything that is not specification text — the test vectors, the reference
checker, and any tooling — is licensed under the MIT licence. See LICENSE-CODE.

That split is deliberate. An implementer copying the test vectors into their
own test suite should not inherit attribution obligations inside their test
files, because that friction is exactly what stops people bothering.
